# kernel-metag.img -- Linux 4.4.302 for Imagination META (TZ1090 "Comet")
#
# Runs on qemu-system-meta -M comet (alias 01sp) from the qemu fork
# (lordrasmus/qemu, branch uclibc-ng); upstream qemu never had META, the
# port comes from Imagination's 1.3.1 branch.  The image is the stripped
# vmlinux; qemu loads it like the Debug Adapter did and builds the boot MMU
# tables itself.  Linux removed metag in 4.17, 4.4.302 is the last LTS.
#
#   qemu-system-meta -M 01sp -nographic -device da,exit_threads=1 \
#     -kernel kernel-metag.img -initrd rootfs.img.xz
#
# The console is the Debug Adapter's channel 1 (ttyDA1); without a chardev
# "chan1" qemu puts it on the first serial, which -nographic makes stdio.
# The machine has 256 MiB.  The command line is built in
# (console=ttyDA1,115200 ro rootfstype=tmpfs metag_da.console_poll=1), the
# initramfs is not: -initrd reaches the kernel through a small device tree
# qemu passes in D0Ar4, with the initrd range in /chosen.
#
# Source: linux-4.4.302.tar.xz from kernel.org.
#
# Patch:
#   kernel-metag-dt-initrd.patch   the kernel reads the initrd range from the
#                                  device tree before it knows meta_memoffset,
#                                  so the bounds stayed physical, and nothing
#                                  reserved the initrd memory; without it an
#                                  initrd from the device tree is not usable
#
# Build, with openadk's metag toolchain (gcc 4.2.4):
#
#   cd linux-4.4.302
#   patch -p1 < kernel-metag-dt-initrd.patch
#   cp kernel-metag.config .config
#   make ARCH=metag CROSS_COMPILE=metag-openadk-linux-uclibc- oldconfig vmlinux
#   metag-openadk-linux-uclibc-strip -o kernel-metag.img vmlinux
#
# The config is openadk's for qemu-metag with the piggyback initramfs taken
# out (INITRAMFS_SOURCE=""), RD_XZ=y for the xz rootfs and CMDLINE_FORCE off.
